From: Abdul Alim <Abdul_Alim1997@live.co.uk>
Sent: 09 February 2026 13:52
To: ManchesterET <manchesterET@Justice.gov.uk>; Stephanie Paton <stephanie.paton@pinsentmasons.com>
Subject: Re: 2406202/2023 Abdul Alim v Royal and Sun Alliance Insurance Limited



Good morning,



Whilst I can appreciate you are experiencing delays, this application is being looked at by Judge Ross. A hearing has been booked for this case already and I was told we'd get a response before then.



Can someone ask Judge Ross directly as to when we can expect a response. The application was a strike out so it's extremely important.



Kind regards,

Abdul Alim

________________________________

From: ManchesterET <manchesterET@Justice.gov.uk<mailto:manchesterET@Justice.gov.uk>>
Sent: 05 February 2026 15:12
To: Abdul Alim <abdul_alim1997@live.co.uk<mailto:abdul_alim1997@live.co.uk>>; Stephanie Paton <stephanie.paton@pinsentmasons.com<mailto:stephanie.paton@pinsentmasons.com>>
Cc: ManchesterET <manchesterET@Justice.gov.uk<mailto:manchesterET@Justice.gov.uk>>
Subject: RE: 2406202/2023 Abdul Alim v Royal and Sun Alliance Insurance Limited



Dear Sir / Madam,



The file and your correspondence has been referred to a Judge for directions, and we will update you as soon as we can.



Due to the large volumes of correspondence already in the system it is not possible to give you a timescale for this.  We are currently experiencing delays of up to 12 weeks in replying to applications.



We are aware of any upcoming Hearing dates and these cases will be given priority



Regards,



Mrs L Chrimes.



